## DATABASE

### Schema summary (key tables)
```sql
shops           — id TEXT, slug, name, type, owner_email, commission_rate, status, is_active
platform_users  — id TEXT, email, password_hash, role, shop_id
services        — id TEXT, shop_id, name, duration_min, price REAL, category, is_active
staff           — id TEXT, shop_id, user_id, display_name, bio, avatar_url, is_active
staff_services  — staff_id, service_id (many-to-many)
schedules       — id TEXT, shop_id, staff_id, day_of_week, start_time, end_time
bookings        — id TEXT, shop_id, staff_id, service_id, customer_name, customer_email, status
invites         — id TEXT, email, shop_id, role, token, expires_at, used_at
contacts        — id TEXT, full_name, shop_name, email, onboarded_at, shop_id
oauth_accounts  — id TEXT, user_id, provider (google|linkedin), provider_user_id
shop_sites      — id TEXT, shop_id, content JSON, theme JSON, status
```

### Query rules
- ALL shop-scoped queries MUST include `WHERE shop_id = ?`
- Never interpolate user input into SQL — use prepared statements only
- Query helpers live in `apps/worker/src/db/queries.ts` — add new ones there, don't inline
- DB type: `DBService` has fields `duration_min` (not `duration_minutes`), `price REAL` (not pence)
- Primary keys are TEXT UUIDs generated with `crypto.randomUUID()`

### Migrations
- Files live in `apps/worker/src/db/migrations/`
- Latest migration: `011_oauth_accounts.sql`
- Next migration number: `012`
- Run with: `npx wrangler d1 execute pivot-parlor-db --remote --file=path/to/migration.sql`

