## API CONVENTIONS

### Worker response envelope (always use this shape)
```typescript
// Success
return c.json({ success: true, data: result })
// Error
return c.json({ success: false, error: "message" }, 400)
```

### API client usage (web side)
```typescript
const api = createApiClient(env.API_URL, token);
const services = await api.get<Service[]>(`/api/shops/${shopId}/services`);
await api.post(`/api/shops/${shopId}/services`, { name, price, duration_min });
await api.put(`/api/shops/${shopId}/services/${id}`, updates);
await api.del(`/api/shops/${shopId}/services/${id}`);
```

### Existing Worker routes
- POST /auth/login, /auth/register, /auth/oauth
- GET/POST/PUT/DELETE /api/shops/:shopId/services
- GET/POST /api/shops/:shopId/staff
- GET/POST /api/shops/:shopId/schedule
- GET /api/shops/:shopId/slots
- GET/POST /api/shops/:shopId/bookings
- POST /api/contact
- POST /api/chat (marketing chatbot — uses OPENROUTER_API_KEY)

